On Mon, 06 Mar 2006 06:18:37 +0000, Jack Bolsen wrote:
> As for wizards, I have 2 wizard ascensions under my belt. Wizards are
> hands down my favorite class. The trick is to not worry about the pet -
> get as much xp as you can, as fast as you can. Doing so builds up spell
> power, which compensates for other shortcomings. It certainly helps to
> have a sleep spell or even an identify spell, but it isn't required. Make
> liberal use of the force bolt spell to kill things at a distance.

Wow.  I play just about the opposit.  Most of my ascentions have been with
wizards (they just rock), and I have to agree that early game is very
difficult.  I try to get to level 2 very quickly and then kinda let things
slide.  I find I have enough mana at XP 2 to handle most situations (yes,
Force Bolt handles most situations), but I try to let my pet eat as much
stuff as possible.  The big threats on DL5-6ish are the hordes of
monsters.  I have three words for thems:  corridors, Force and Bolt.

I find the mines are rather more dangerous - not as much useful ways to
confine monsters...but if you have enough mana...  However, your starting
dagger (I'll sometimes poke into the mines to get an early one and train
it up smacking lichens around) is enough to kill one or two gnomes, even
with no armor, and having a pet around means you won't have to deal with
many of them.  The big threats are what you save massive Foce Bolt
barrages for.

I tend to stick to the main levels if I can get to Sokoban early.  But if
I'm hitting dl7 and haven't seen the entrance yet, I'll turn back and head
for minetown.

I've started playing more with stacks of daggers, and they're certainly
awesome...but playing as a pacifist when possible and using force bolt
when it's not - that's my way to deal with it :)

Main goals:
Sokoban for food
Mines for magic missle.

